# PortBar

macOS menu bar app (Tauri 2 + vanilla TypeScript) that lists TCP ports in LISTEN
state with process name / PID and can kill the owning process.

## Layout

- `src/` — frontend (Vite, no framework)
  - `types.ts` mirrors Rust structs; `api.ts` is the only place calling `invoke`/`listen`
  - `main.ts` owns state + DOM rendering
  - `i18n.ts` zh/en message bundles; locale comes from the `system_locale` command
  - `format.ts` pure display helpers (shortened command line, `~` paths)
- `src-tauri/src/`
  - `ports.rs` — pure domain logic: `lsof`/`ps` parsing, signal sending (unit-tested)
  - `system.rs` — open URL / Finder, clipboard; URLs are built in Rust (localhost only)
  - `commands.rs` — thin `#[tauri::command]` wrappers, run work on `spawn_blocking`
  - `tray.rs` — tray icon, menu, panel toggle/positioning
  - `error.rs` — `AppError`, serialized as `{ code, pid?, detail? }`
  - `locale.rs` — system language detection (`sys-locale`)
  - `lib.rs` — builder wiring only

## Contracts

- Adding a command: implement in `ports.rs` → wrap in `commands.rs` → register in
  `generate_handler!` → add typed wrapper in `src/api.ts` → mirror types in `src/types.ts`.
- Rust structs use `#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]`; TS types must match exactly.
- Event names are constants on both sides (`panel-shown`).

## Commands

- `pnpm tauri dev` — run app; `pnpm build` — typecheck + bundle frontend
- `cargo test --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml` — Rust unit tests
- `cargo clippy --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml -- -D warnings`
- `pnpm tauri build` — produce `.app` / `.dmg`

## Before finishing a change

Run `pnpm build`, `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` and `cargo test`; all must pass.
